Task 1: Enable proxy and proxy_http modules on Debian and Suse systems
Description Task 1: Enable the proxy and proxy_http modules for Apache on Debian and Suse systems to support reverse proxy functionality.

Task 2: Configure locations using a template
Description Task 2: Use the location.conf.j2 template to configure Apache location blocks, setting the destination file and mode for each location defined in the httpd_locations variable. Notify the httpd configuration test and restart handler after configuration.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook:
---
- name: Enable proxy and proxy_http modules on Debian and Suse systems
  apache2_module:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop:
    - proxy
    - proxy_http
  when: ansible_os_family in ['Debian', 'Suse']

- name: Configure locations using a template
  template:
    src: location.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/apache2/conf-available/location.conf
  notify:
    - Test Apache configuration
    - Restart Apache
  vars:
    httpd_locations: "{{ httpd_locations | default([]) }}"


